<div class="wrap page-head">
  <p class="eyebrow">Global Program · 3 weeks to 3 months</p>
  <h1>For families passing through Hội An</h1>
  <p class="lede">Not everyone follows a school calendar. If you are travelling, here for a season, or between schools, your child can join us for three weeks to three months. They join a real class with our regular students, not a separate holiday group.</p>
</div>

<section class="band--paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Four ways to join</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <p class="program__ages">Ages 2 to 5</p>
        <h3>Early Years</h3>
        <p>Play-based days in English following the British EYFS framework. Stories, music, movement, sand, water. Short-term children settle in quickly because the days are predictable and warm.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="program__ages">Years 1 to 9 · half day</p>
        <h3>Vocational half day</h3>
        <p>For children who learn by doing. Cooking and nutrition, public speaking, creative play and innovation, PE and movement, art and design. Making, not sitting.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="program__ages">Years 1 to 9 · half day</p>
        <h3>Academic half day</h3>
        <p>Keep up with school while you are away. Cambridge English, Maths, and Science in small classes, without committing to a full day.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="program__ages">Years 1 to 9 · full day</p>
        <h3>Cambridge plus vocational, full day</h3>
        <p>The whole PRA day: Cambridge core subjects in the morning and vocational classes in the afternoon. This is what our regular students do.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% set riverColor = "var(--sand)" %}{% include "partials/river.njk" %}

<section>
  <div class="wrap two">
    <div>
      <h2>What you go home with</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A written progress report within the first two weeks, so you know how your child is settling.</li>
        <li>A final report at the end of the stay.</li>
        <li>A Certificate of Completion. Useful for the school back home, and nice on the fridge.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What it costs</h2>
      <p>From 4,200,000 VND per week when you book ten weeks or more. Shorter stays cost a little more per week. The full table is on the <a href="{{ '/admissions/tuition-and-fees/' | url }}">fees page</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="photo photo--blob-b" data-caption="photo: a Global Program student at a cooking class with regular students"></div>
  </div>
</section>

